# AI-Driven Supply Chain Optimization — Full Project Report

> **Author:** Shubh  
> **Stack:** Python 3.14 · PyTorch · XGBoost · Statsmodels · FastAPI · Streamlit · Optuna  
> **Data:** DataCo Smart Supply Chain · Historical Product Demand · Olist Brazilian E-Commerce

---

## 1. Project Overview

This project builds an **end-to-end, production-ready AI supply chain system** that solves three core business problems simultaneously:

| Business Problem | AI Solution |
|---|---|
| "How much demand will we see next week?" | Time-series forecasting (SARIMA + XGBoost + LSTM) |
| "What's the cheapest way to deliver all orders?" | Vehicle Routing Optimization (Greedy NN VRP) |
| "How much stock should we hold per SKU?" | EOQ + Safety Stock + ABC Classification + Stockout RF |

The system wraps all outputs in a **REST API (FastAPI)** and a **live interactive dashboard (Streamlit)**, making every model's predictions queryable in real-time.

---

## 2. Datasets

### 2.1 DataCo Smart Supply Chain (`DataCoSupplyChainDataset.csv`)
- **Size:** 180,519 rows × 53 columns (cleaned to 58 after feature engineering)
- **Content:** Order-level records — product categories, shipping modes, scheduled vs actual delivery days, sales revenue, profit per order
- **Key columns used:** `Sales`, `Benefit per order`, `Days for shipment (scheduled)`, `Days for shipping (real)`, `Shipping Mode`, `Category Name`, `order date (DateOrders)`
- **Data quality:** Columns with >40% null values dropped; numeric nulls filled with column median

### 2.2 Historical Product Demand (`Historical Product Demand.csv`)
- **Size:** 634,553 rows × 4 columns (after grouping and cleaning)
- **Content:** Daily demand records per product SKU per warehouse
- **Key columns:** `Product_Code`, `Warehouse`, `Date`, `Order_Demand`
- **Special cleaning:** `Order_Demand` contained parenthesized negatives (e.g., `(500)`) which were stripped to numeric
- **Unique SKUs:** 2,160 products across 4 warehouses (Whse_A, Whse_B, Whse_C, Whse_J)

### 2.3 Olist Brazilian E-Commerce (7 relational files)
- **Orders:** 99,441 orders × 8 columns
- **Order Items:** 112,650 line items × 7 columns
- **Geolocation:** 1,000,163 records × 5 columns (zip prefix → lat/lng)
- **Used for:** Customer zip-level demand aggregation and delivery route planning across Brazil
- **Joined geo-demand stops:** 14,820 unique delivery locations with known coordinates

