### Phase 4 — Inventory Optimisation

**Model 1 — Economic Order Quantity (EOQ):**
```
EOQ = sqrt( (2 × Annual_Demand × Ordering_Cost) / Holding_Cost )

Parameters:
  Ordering_Cost    = $50 per order
  Holding_Cost_Pct = 20% of unit cost/year
  Avg_Unit_Cost    = $10
  Holding_Cost     = $2/unit/year
```

**Model 2 — Safety Stock & Reorder Point:**
```
Service Level = 95%  →  Z-score = 1.645

Safety_Stock = Z × sqrt(
    Lead_Time × std_demand²  +  (avg_demand × std_lead_time)²
)

Reorder_Point = avg_demand × Lead_Time + Safety_Stock

Parameters:
  Lead_Time       = 7 days
  Lead_Time_Std   = 2 days
```

**Model 3 — ABC Classification:**
```
A-class:  cumulative revenue ≤ 80%   →  85 SKUs  (top 3.9%)
B-class:  cumulative revenue ≤ 95%   → 203 SKUs  (next 9.4%)
C-class:  cumulative revenue > 95%   → 1872 SKUs (tail 86.7%)
```

**Model 4 — Stockout Risk Classifier (Random Forest):**
```python
RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, max_depth=8, class_weight='balanced')

Features: Order_Item_Quantity, Days_for_shipment_scheduled,
          Days_for_shipping_real, order_month, order_quarter,
          Shipping_Mode_*, Category_Name_*

Label: stockout_risk = (days_real > days_scheduled × 1.5)
```

**Results (actual run):**
| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| SKUs analysed | 2,160 |
| Class A SKUs | 85 |
| Class B SKUs | 203 |
| Class C SKUs | 1,872 |
| Classifier Accuracy | 100% (F1=1.00 on 36,104 test samples) |
| Test support (no stockout) | 26,166 |
| Test support (stockout) | 9,938 |

**Saved:** `reports/inventory_plan.csv`

